Keep BaseMemStream::makeSubStream() inside the buffer.

makeSubStream() stored an unchecked start offset, so bufPtr = buf + startA
pointed outside the buffer for a startxref beyond the end of the file (e.g.
"startxref 4294967295"). On 64-bit hosts that pointer is past bufEnd and the
stream reads as empty, but on 32-bit hosts buf + 4294967295 wraps to buf - 1:
the xref parser reads one byte before the buffer and, because setPos() clamps
to the same bogus start, re-parses the file from there endlessly, creating
LZW filter chains until the guest runs out of memory (bad_alloc in
Stream::makeFilter < Parser::makeStream < XRef::readXRef). A negative start
would read before the buffer on any host. Map out-of-range starts to an empty
stream at the end of the buffer.

Regression test cpp/tests/poppler-memstream-substream-test.cpp makes
substreams of a 3-byte MemStream at offsets -1 (where buf + 4294967295 points
on 32-bit hosts), 4 and 4294967295; without the fix the ones at -1 read the
byte in front of the buffer.

Not fixed upstream as of 9182fd5.
Upstream: none found (poppler/poppler issues and MRs searched for
makeSubStream, MemStream, startxref).

